{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm","id":1300972,"title":"Four levels of Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-29T16:03:54-07:00","id":1300972,"title":"Four levels of Paradigm","content":"The following may be obvious, but I don't think it gets explicitly talked about this way very often. Too much emphasis tends to be placed on Tradition Paradigm or Tradition subgroup paradigm.<br /> <br /> It helps to talk about Paradigm as kind of step pyramid with layers of increasing specificity. A lot of the following only applies to Tradition mages.<br /> <br /> At the base level is Purple Paradigm. Some sense that magic is partly based on belief is necessary for Tradition Mages to cooperate without being shaken to their core every time they see their comrades do magic.<br /> <br /> Next is Tradition Paradigm. Traditions are broader than they tend to be depicted; they're not single cultures, but agglomerations of different cultures and practices with similar philosophy who are allied out of convenience because of the Technocratic threat. You can see this most easily with the Hermetics and Dreamspeakers, but it is true for all of them. Yet, there tends to be unifying themes and stylistic influences that most of their members will follow.<br /> <br /> Within Traditions are the subgroups and individual chantries. A Mage will probably identify more with their House or tribe or coven or secret fraternal organization than with their Tradition. The sub-group will probably inform their Paradigm far more as well.<br /> <br /> Finally, all magic is ultimately individual. In modern individualistic societies, no two mages will do magic alike. This is very important to explain to new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T03:24:41-07:00","id":1301049,"title":"","content":"I like the M20 approach where you pick your own personal Paradigm, and your own Practice, and your own Instruments, and which Tradition you fit into is then another matter to consider. I like how each Tradition has a good few Paradigms linked to them. You can have 50 million different types of Hermetics who don't agree totally on Paradigm, Practice and Instruments.<br /> <br /> Another thing I like to do is add complexity to Paradigm as Arete increases.<br /> <br /> Ancient Languages hold all answers.<br /> <br /> Ancient Languages hold all answers, and when we use them we turn the keys to reality.<br /> <br /> Reality is linguistic, and ancient languages hold special significance and power; when we use them we turn the keys to reality.<br /> <br /> Reality is linguistic, and ancient languages hold special significance and power; when we use them we turn the keys to reality. And if we can recall the language of creation, the languages of the gods, we can ascend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:59:14-07:00","id":1301395,"title":"","content":"I view it as somewhat the opposite. Your paradigm begins as an elaborate structure of the world that is simply an 'alternative personal consensus' then slowly breaks down as you gain arete and realize that rules aren't necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:56:22-07:00","id":1301416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301395#post1301395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I view it as somewhat the opposite. Your paradigm begins as an elaborate structure of the world that is simply an 'alternative personal consensus' then slowly breaks down as you gain arete and realize that rules aren't necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing M20 tried to move away from is this idea that you almost lose your Paradigm and it just becomes Purple Paradigm at high Arete. High Arete reflects a deeper and more intimate understanding of your Paradigm. And that can include adding in nuance about Belief and Will pushing Reality, but the idea that you started with (Creation is Divine and Alive, Reality is an Illusion, All Reality is Consciousness, We Are Gods in Disguise) should still be the thematic core of your focus.<br /> <br /> So an Arete 9 Shaman can just will Spirits into whatever shape she likes, but she doesn't do that because respecting the natural order is a big deal for her. If she were the sort of person who did that, she wouldn't be an Arete 9 &quot;all our power comes from the spirits&quot; Shaman. That sort of brash mistreatment just doesn't suit her, it's the opposite of what she is. And she could work without Focus on practically everything, but she uses her Focus all the time because it's important to her. She loves her Practice, she loves her tools, she loves the nuanced relationships she has built with the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Basically I think it's good (and I think M20 is mostly agreed with me) that Mage's are allowed to become *more* linked to their Focus in some ways as they ascend, even as they reach a point where they know they don't technically need it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:38:29-07:00","id":1301432,"title":"","content":"And frankly, I could fit my respect for M20's view of the magic system into a thimble.<br /> <br /> High Arete doesn't reflect anything with regards to your paradigm, it reflects your growing power and deeper understanding of the world, your paradigm is merely an interface for that understanding which is important as it colors everything you do... but your paradigm doesn't shift or change just because you gained a dot of Arete. And quite honestly, I find M20's view of paradigm as particularly frustrating, as it reduces what is meant to be an all encompassing world view to a few convenient soundbites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:45:12-07:00","id":1301523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301432#post1301432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Arete doesn't reflect anything with regards to your paradigm, it reflects your growing power and deeper understanding of the world, your paradigm is merely an interface for that understanding which is important as it colors everything you do... but your paradigm doesn't shift or change just because you gained a dot of Arete.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That... depends entirely on a lot of other factors, depending on edition and which books and items you allow into play.<br /> <br /> For example, with the Resonance system (from Revised and M20, but pretty backwards compatible, IMO), your ability to work certain magics will change as you gain Resonance. And one way to gain Resonance is through a Seeking getting intense - in other words, going up in Arete can change how your magic is flavored. Now, that itself doesn't directly change your worldview, but it can subtly affect it, especially when using sensory powers - if you suddenly gain a trait of &quot;Electric&quot; resonance, you are going to find it easier to sense things that could fit as &quot;electric&quot; - from actual electricity with Forces to an &quot;electric&quot; emotional connection between two lovers or potential lovers with Mind, Spirit, or Time (in the case of potential lovers, seeing the future) - and less easy to sense things that could be considered the opposite of electric - resistant materials such as rubber, stagnant romances, and so on. Depending on how far you and your ST choose to take the effects, that can slowly change your world-view in certain ways. That may not change your full, fundamental beliefs, but it can change little beliefs, which in turn can shift bigger ones as they filter your perception.<br /> <br /> Also, there's a merit in &quot;Masters of the Art&quot; that presents an alternative view. &quot;Ascension Message&quot; is a five dot merit that says that you'll never become an Archmage. Ever. You can have Arete 10 and will never raise any sphere above 5. Why is this a merit? Because the view of Archmastery presented in the book is one of shortcomings - becoming and Archmage can hamper your ability to interact with the mortal world, and can hold back actual understanding that leads to Ascension. You become so focused on your power that you hamper your ability to actually go beyond it - you are trapped in the limits of your paradigm, cannot interact with the Consensus without risking Paradox by existing, and thus have a harder time leading the world to Ascension. However, an Archmage who realizes this can program their Avatar to avoid learning those higher levels of power. Instead, as your Arete increases beyond five, you find yourself able to incorporate alternative paradigms into your magic. The exact mechanical effects aren't defined, but this likely is similar to merits like Techgnosi (Revised Chorus TradBook), Dual Tradition, and similar sources, where you develop additional tools that you can use, break out of the limits your paradigm might have on certain types of magic more easily, and possibly develop other benefits that might come from having the ability to reconcile multiple worldviews (if nothing else, it makes you a killer diplomat). <br /> <br /> Of course, you may not include that merit in your game or may not have even been aware of it, or you may just never have liked it and leave it out, and that will change your view on magic and paradigms and how they work, but it is an option, and as such someone who is familiar with it and especially has played with it in the past may use that as the basis for their own paradigm understanding - that enlightenment and skill can and should change your view of how the world works and thus change your magical viewpoints and abilities. Your game may run as you wish it to, but it is important to realize that deeper enlightenment CAN lead to a change in paradigm per mechanics that exist in the game as a whole (if not the modern version).<br /> <br /> I also disagree that M20 changed paradigm from &quot;an all-encompassing worldview to a few convenient soundbites&quot; - or rather, they did, but they didn't. They changed the order of terms, turning Paradigms into the conceptual bases upon which your Focus is now built, and using the term Focus where Paradigm was used before. In my read, the game changed which words were used for which things rather than changing the system, and added in the added element of &quot;pick a few of these phrases that help define your worldview&quot; along with tools and practices and tradition. The same concept still exists, it's just that different words refer to different things. Again, YMMV and I may have missed what you specifically were criticizing, but the change in terms did come up elsewhere in another thread and I do feel it's important to lay that out and make sure everyone's on the same page so we don't miss each other's points.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> I will disagree on the exact order of the pyramid myself in my mind. I do think Purple Paradigm (never heard that before but I like it) is a sort of base of the philosophy of Mage magick, but I think that your character's circumstances may be an important factor. A character who is taken in quickly by an Tradition or (more likely) Convention may find their own viewpoint warped or conditioned to match or jive with that group - the Traditions may be more willing to set you loose and put you with someone else if they can if your existing view is too alien to their practices, but if you are isolated or brought in by less scrupulous traditionalists, you may not get as much freedom and may find yourself forced into their view. Likewise, the Technocrats are likely to try and pair you with a Convention that fits your existing world view most closely, but there will most likely be some conditioning and shaping of beliefs. That said, I do think personal paradigm does need more time to shine.<br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> As a side note, I recently was rereading the Pentex Subsidiaries section on Black Dog Games and remembered a bit about Warlock: the Pretension's &quot;Guide to Paradigm Infliction (Level Four) and thought this may have been a discussion about that...<br /> <br /> Also as a separate side note, I just realized in my first section that the rules you choose and don't choose to use in a game are actually a possible tool to explain Paradigm/Focus to new Mage gamers... Your view on a game is going to be very different if you use only the core book instead of supplements, if you focus on one edition's materials or mechanics rather than another's (in as much as they are compatible), and what you choose to cut out or alter and what you choose to keep. May need to look at this idea again when I've slept...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:17:14-07:00","id":1301540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301432#post1301432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And frankly, I could fit my respect for M20's view of the magic system into a thimble.<br /> <br /> High Arete doesn't reflect anything with regards to your paradigm, it reflects your growing power and deeper understanding of the world, your paradigm is merely an interface for that understanding which is important as it colors everything you do... but your paradigm doesn't shift or change just because you gained a dot of Arete. And quite honestly, I find M20's view of paradigm as particularly frustrating, as it reduces what is meant to be an all encompassing world view to a few convenient soundbites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it really does. If you're a Tech Holds All Answers Mage, improving your Arete absolutely reflects developing a greater understanding of the technological (technomagickal?) aspects of reality. And as your Arete improves and you start dropping tools, you absolutely need a way to justify your belief. At the end of the day in Mage, you have to answer &quot;Does My Mage Believe They Can Do This?&quot; before casting an effect. If the answer is no, they often can't (although sometimes this will simply make it Vulgar instead of making it impossible). Belief, Paradigm and Focus (Focus being Paradigm + Practice + Instruments) remain important at all levels of mastery.<br /> <br /> As for the Paradigm shifting and becoming more nuanced, this is a natural consequence of learning more about reality. If a Mage believes that all reality is Consciousness, then as they improve their mastery, and their control of Correspondence, they'll naturally begin to shift more into &quot;The only true Reality is Consciousness, and all minds are linked / all minds are one / all minds are fragments of one whole / etc.&quot; Even if the player still only has &quot;All reality is Consciousness&quot; written on their sheet, their Paradigm absolutely has shifted since they've had to make it more sophisticated to accommodate things like being able to visit the dreams of other people (something they can do at Arete 3) as opposed to just strengthening their own mind and understanding the superficial emotions of those around them (what they can do at Arete 1). And at Arete 9, such a Mage will be incredibly invested in these ideas, even if they've overcome the need to use most of their Instruments. Paradigm forms the core of their worldview by this point; they haven't lost their Paradigm to embrace some meta vanilla concept of Belief Shapes Reality.<br /> <br /> As for M20 reducing Paradigm to soundbites... I mean it gives an in-depth writeup for each of the common Paradigms, plus some rare/intriguing ones in Book of Secrets, but go off I guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T03:38:26-07:00","id":1301566,"title":"","content":"I always see the Paradigm &lt;&gt; Arete relation being able to go both ways.<br /> It highly depends on the characer in question, but the way a Mage can grow in Arete to me is either what Enginseer mentioned - namely the Mage more and more letting go of of the rigidity of their paradigm as they learn more about reality, becoming more flexible and loose and also dropping instruments that way...gaining a more universal flexiblity and understanding. A Mage is though never without paradigm - they always believe in *something*.<br /> <br /> OR the Mage goes the opposite way:<br /> They become more and more involved in the intricacies of their very Paradigm, and instead of letting go of parts of it they make it more elaborate, more intricate, more involved. Essentially instead of relaxing their Paradigm to encompass the new things they learn, they go the opposite direction and build up more and more paradigmic structures to make more and more things work in the confines of their paradigm.<br /> Of course some would say that they become entrapped in it, and Exemplars are probably the extreme of this path.<br /> But the way the dropping of instruments in this case works, to me, is akin to the Mage more and more believing that they are an enlightened master - nay, harbinger - of their paradigm, or get more and more favored by the Old Gods they worship, etc. etc.<br /> Whatever form their paradigm takes shape, they are such an icon of it, they need the handholding less and less.<br /> <br /> Two directly opposing paths, two completely different direction or mindsets, but both can be a mirror of raising Arete and dropping the tools. The only Mages that don't grow in Arete and flexibility are those that stand still and don't change in any direction. That is the key. A lack of evolution in any way. A lack of growth, no matter what shape that growth takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-01-2019, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:34:13-07:00","id":1301588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301566#post1301566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always see the Paradigm &lt;&gt; Arete relation being able to go both ways.<br /> It highly depends on the characer in question, but the way a Mage can grow in Arete to me is either what Enginseer mentioned - namely the Mage more and more letting go of of the rigidity of their paradigm as they learn more about reality, becoming more flexible and loose and also dropping instruments that way...gaining a more universal flexiblity and understanding. A Mage is though never without paradigm - they always believe in *something*.<br /> <br /> OR the Mage goes the opposite way:<br /> They become more and more involved in the intricacies of their very Paradigm, and instead of letting go of parts of it they make it more elaborate, more intricate, more involved. Essentially instead of relaxing their Paradigm to encompass the new things they learn, they go the opposite direction and build up more and more paradigmic structures to make more and more things work in the confines of their paradigm.<br /> Of course some would say that they become entrapped in it, and Exemplars are probably the extreme of this path.<br /> But the way the dropping of instruments in this case works, to me, is akin to the Mage more and more believing that they are an enlightened master - nay, harbinger - of their paradigm, or get more and more favored by the Old Gods they worship, etc. etc.<br /> Whatever form their paradigm takes shape, they are such an icon of it, they need the handholding less and less.<br /> <br /> Two directly opposing paths, two completely different direction or mindsets, but both can be a mirror of raising Arete and dropping the tools. The only Mages that don't grow in Arete and flexibility are those that stand still and don't change in any direction. That is the key. A lack of evolution in any way. A lack of growth, no matter what shape that growth takes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. I wish something like this were written in the M20 corebook.<br /> <br /> Because you can see Mages going in both directions; the Etherite who becomes like a mad parody of the Union, trying to quantify EVERYTHING, pin it down, define it, measure it, understand it, overcome it. Making grand theories that summarize everything. And the Etherite who accepts more and more that in a world of gods and monsters, his own scientific understanding is abstract, a means by which he overcomes Reality and imposes his will. Those are the two extremes, and both have some importance.<br /> <br /> What is bad, though, is how some old editions of Mage did have this subtle idea that the Focus/Paradigm was &quot;fake&quot;, and that Mages would wake up to the One True Paradigm as they got closer to Ascension, letting go of everything that makes them unique and thematic and cool, and becoming a simple Purple Paradigm Mage. I'm glad that modern Mage has a lot of nuance in what it means to increase Arete, how it can reflect anything from letting go of your past to becoming more cruel to overcoming intricate formulae, whatever path your Avatar offers (or you make it offer?) is a path to ascension in one way or another.<br /> <br /> In the game I'm STing currently a Mage who believes he is the chosen one is guided by an Avatar that has taken inspiration from the Mage's delusions. If you're the chosen one, I'll give you prophecies to fulfill, obstacles to overcome, villains to defeat, I'll show you the path to understanding the ancient languages you love to decipher... in the end this Avatar will become Manifest and take the form of a dangerous villain, and while it won't kill anyone directly the resulting conflict may cause deaths. Regardless, the PC in question will improve Arete by further investing in this &quot;chosen one&quot; ideal, and further understanding his investment in ancient texts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T09:36:50-07:00","id":1301659,"title":"","content":"What I like about M20 is that it allows for both approaches. Sure, it favors the \u201cembrace your truth!\u201d approach that is in many ways antithetical to the earlier editions' \u201cLet it go!\u201d approach; but with the inclusion of the \u201cWe Are Gods In Disguise\u201d Paradigm in <b>Book of Secrets</b>, you get to nestle the old approach inside the newer approach: \u201cWe Are Gods In Disguise\u201d is the Purple Paradigm with a different name; and as you embrace that Paradigm, everything else falls by the wayside. <br /> <br /> All that said, my personal head canon is that \u201cWe Are Gods In Disguise\u201d was an innovation of the Traditions, is the glue that holds the Traditions together, and outside of the Traditions is most often found among Orphans, the Hollow Ones (who until recently were affiliated with the Traditions), and the Batini (who helped develop it back when they helped found the Traditions): other Disparates have a tendency to view their own faction's philosophy as paramount, and the Technocracy treats \u201cWe Are Gods In Disguise\u201d as antithetical to their own theories. Put another way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1503_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1503\" data-vbnamecard=\"1503\">Faradn</a>'s proposed pyramid only really exists for the Traditions and their allies/expatriates; the Disparates in general top out their pyramids at the faction level, and the Technocracy has its own alternative to the Purple Paradigm capping their pyramid. <br /> <br /> And that's my other problem with the earlier editions' approach: by making the Purple Paradigm a fundamental truth of the setting, they made it impossible to play nearly anyone who wasn't affiliated with the Traditions in some way without them either being liars, ignorant, or both. This <i>especially</i> applied to the Union, but wasn't unique to them. Which is fine if you're going with \u201cTraditions good; Technocracy bad; and everyone else is dumb\u201d in your campaign. But if you want anything more nuanced than that, you can't have the Purple Paradigm as an incontrovertible truth of the setting. <br /> <br /> Which is why I like the fact that it's \u201cjust another Paradigm\u201d in M20 (though given its significance to the Traditions, I really wish it had been featured in the core book rather than the companion book). It goes along with M20's dethroning the Traditions as <i>the</i> protagonists of the game, and allows for other factions, or even independent mages, to be put front and center. Ironically, the game is more flexible this way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-01-2019, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:25:39-07:00","id":1301679,"title":"","content":"Also, one of my hacks is to take the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1190573-redefining-mystics-and-technomancers\">technomancer/mystic divide</a> and reformulate it as an external/internal divide, depending on whether the mage believes that what he can do comes from within or without. \u201cWe Are Gods in Disguise\u201d pretty much requires an Internal Focus, and the Technocracy\u2019s counterpart similarly requires an External Focus, which is why the division is generally conceived in terms of mysticism vs. technomancy (as the majority of the Traditions have mystical paradigms and nearly all of the Union has technomantic paradigms). But for the purpose of this thread, the important part of that hack is how it addresses Instruments: if you have an Internal Focus, you\u2019re able to discard your Instruments as your Arete increases; if you have an External Focus, you instead come to master your Instruments: you can never work your will without them (as they\u2019re what connects you to whatever the source of your power is), but you get especially adept at wielding them as your Arete improves, letting you get more out of them than an Internalist could ever hope to achieve. <br /> <br /> Being a hack, it\u2019s not Rules as Written; but it\u2019s very much in keeping with the view that I outlined in my last post, and I do think it\u2019s largely in keeping with M20\u2019s overall philosophy of Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:48:00-07:00","id":1302099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301540#post1301540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, it really does. If you're a Tech Holds All Answers Mage, improving your Arete absolutely reflects developing a greater understanding of the technological (technomagickal?) aspects of reality. And as your Arete improves and you start dropping tools, you absolutely need a way to justify your belief. At the end of the day in Mage, you have to answer &quot;Does My Mage Believe They Can Do This?&quot; before casting an effect. If the answer is no, they often can't (although sometimes this will simply make it Vulgar instead of making it impossible). Belief, Paradigm and Focus (Focus being Paradigm + Practice + Instruments) remain important at all levels of mastery.<br /> <br /> As for the Paradigm shifting and becoming more nuanced, this is a natural consequence of learning more about reality. If a Mage believes that all reality is Consciousness, then as they improve their mastery, and their control of Correspondence, they'll naturally begin to shift more into &quot;The only true Reality is Consciousness, and all minds are linked / all minds are one / all minds are fragments of one whole / etc.&quot; Even if the player still only has &quot;All reality is Consciousness&quot; written on their sheet, their Paradigm absolutely has shifted since they've had to make it more sophisticated to accommodate things like being able to visit the dreams of other people (something they can do at Arete 3) as opposed to just strengthening their own mind and understanding the superficial emotions of those around them (what they can do at Arete 1). And at Arete 9, such a Mage will be incredibly invested in these ideas, even if they've overcome the need to use most of their Instruments. Paradigm forms the core of their worldview by this point; they haven't lost their Paradigm to embrace some meta vanilla concept of Belief Shapes Reality.<br /> <br /> As for M20 reducing Paradigm to soundbites... I mean it gives an in-depth writeup for each of the common Paradigms, plus some rare/intriguing ones in Book of Secrets, but go off I guess <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And that's just it. 'Tech Holds all the Answers' isn't a paradigm. In any shape or form. Tech Holds All the Answers is a convenient soundbite, with an extended explanation that literally amounts to 'You can use concrete techniques and tools to affect changes in the universe.' But that doesn't answer or even ASK the question of why? Why does the Raygun work? What principals does it work on? Does it work on the principle that it looks machine-ish and has a trigger and a weird laser-y looking doohicky on the front? Does it pull orgonne energy from a power cell you charged by syphoning power from a brothel and convert it into beams of burning light? If Orgonne Energy can be collected and made use of, what else does that mean for our mages worldview? What other properties does this energy source have and what rules does it follow?<br /> <br /> Literally EVERY paradigm uses tools and techniques to affect changes in the world. And MOST of M20's paradigms are similarly shallow. With a tiny few that work as actual paradigms.<br /> <br /> Secondly. Your Arete has little to do with your understanding of your paradigm. Again, if you were the sort of person to adjust your paradigm to new information, you wouldn't be a mage at all. You'd be a sleeper.<br /> <br /> Arete is your base ability. Like strength, or intelligence. It represents your innate ability to work with magic. SPHERE levels, have to do with skill in using it for specific tasks, but in the end, it's no more worldview changing than any OTHER skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T01:14:55-07:00","id":1302138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1301659#post1301659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's my other problem with the earlier editions' approach: by making the Purple Paradigm a fundamental truth of the setting, they made it impossible to play nearly anyone who wasn't affiliated with the Traditions in some way without them either being liars, ignorant, or both. This <i>especially</i> applied to the Union, but wasn't unique to them. Which is fine if you're going with \u201cTraditions good; Technocracy bad; and everyone else is dumb\u201d in your campaign. But if you want anything more nuanced than that, you can't have the Purple Paradigm as an incontrovertible truth of the setting.<br /> <br /> Which is why I like the fact that it's \u201cjust another Paradigm\u201d in M20 (though given its significance to the Traditions, I really wish it had been featured in the core book rather than the companion book). It goes along with M20's dethroning the Traditions as <i>the</i> protagonists of the game, and allows for other factions, or even independent mages, to be put front and center. Ironically, the game is more flexible this way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed; Reality being negotiable is a good feature of Mage. If a person believes that the Universe is entirely rational and understandable, they're at least partly right. And if a person believes that the Universe is chaotic and impossible to truly understand, they're at least partly right. A big feature of the Ascension War is that the answers to these questions aren't settled yet; Reality just isn't homogeneous enough for that, with separate Reality Zones all over the world accommodating contradictory ideas.<br /> <br /> These beliefs aren't just tools for using magick, they're deep-seated beliefs about the nature of Reality, and some of that goes down to faith. It's good if the ST keeps the &quot;truth&quot; of the setting ambiguous, perhaps even letting Mages see what they expect to see in some cases (ESPECIALLY in the Spirit World, but also with extremely esoteric applications of Level 1 Spheres; Mages are perfectly capable of deluding themselves as much as anything).<br /> <br /> Of course some things do need to objectively exist within a setting. The Low Umbra definitely exists, but what it truly IS is a matter of belief. The underworld? A hell that traps souls that are still bound to our world? The gateway to oblivion? A shadow of our world, full of post-life-echoes of living people? What's important in Mage is that the strict scientist who discovers the Umbra for the first time can, once they get over the denial, incorporate it into their own ideas and come up with an argument that no one can falsify, and works for them. &quot;Well these look like ghosts, but that's absurd. They're just psionic imprints left by particularly distraught and emotional people before their death.&quot; &quot;These 'spirits' are simply aliens that inhabit weaker subdimensions that seek to feed off of our own&quot;.<br /> <br /> So while the ST can say &quot;yes you can meet Thor in the High Umbra&quot;, what that actually MEANS has no fixed answer. Is he a true god? Does he exist to inspire faith? Or does he exist because of faith? Is he part of The One, an avatar or aspect of it? Is he a shared hallucination of the Mages who meet him? Is he a powerful Spirit that has learned to feed off of a religion? Did Germanic Mages/Sleepers create these &quot;Gods&quot;, deliberately or accidentally? So even the objective facts of the setting remain contentious points of debate and argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-03-2019, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T01:19:16-07:00","id":1302139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1302099#post1302099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arete is your base ability. Like strength, or intelligence. It represents your innate ability to work with magic. SPHERE levels, have to do with skill in using it for specific tasks, but in the end, it's no more worldview changing than any OTHER skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah.<br /> But, what *is* Arete? You're saying what it allows the character to do, yes - i.e. develop more sphere knowledge - but you are not saying what exactly happens/changes inside the character when their Arete increases. &quot;They can do magic betterer&quot; is the result, not the cause.<br /> <br /> And if the answer to that is &quot;It means they know more about magick&quot;, it's an absurdly simplified answer, due to my next point;<br /> Consider that Arete gets increased not by some person sitting down with you and telling you &quot;Aight, so here is how this works...&quot; - that's a way to go about learning Spheres, not Arete - but by going though Seekings, Avatar-driven events that are supposed to <i>fundamentally challenge the Mage's current perceptions and/or to expand them.</i><br /> Saying that Arete has no effect on Paradigm and vice versa is, to me, rather baffling.<br /> <br /> Again, Seekings, the event that makes an increase of Arete possible, either challenge or try to push for an expansion of the Mage's fundamental perceptions of themselves, the world and magick - and that's exactly what Paradigm *is*.<br /> <br /> And thus, by conclusion, a Mage who does not modify their worldview in some way, cannot increase in Arete - because a lack of Paradigmic change, either loosening or refinement, is exactly what makes you fail Seekings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-03-2019, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T01:28:29-07:00","id":1302140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1302139#post1302139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the answer to that is &quot;It means they know more about magick&quot;, it's an absurdly simplified answer, due to my next point;<br /> Consider that Arete gets increased not by some person sitting down with you and telling you &quot;Aight, so here is how this works...&quot; - that's a way to go about learning Spheres, not Arete - but by going though Seekings, Avatar-driven events that are supposed to <i>fundamentally challenge the Mage's current perceptions and/or to expand them</i>, saying that Arete has no effect on Paradigm and vice versa is, to me, rather baffling.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is made even more explicit with Grimoires; if you increase your Arete with a Grimoire you literally have to devote weeks to poring over every detail until you understand the esoteric messages hidden within. That requires understanding and the ability to accept the new ideas being presented (so long as these new ideas fit into your wider understanding). And because of that you need to roll Intelligence + Esoterica/Science, Perception + Research, Wits + Occult/Technology, perhaps even Stamina + Academics or Perception + Art, or Stamina + Martial Arts/Yoga/Meditation, and all sorts of other rolls to actually decipher a Grimoire. One of the suggested challenges in Seekings is that the ST gives the player similar rolls to complete, at appropriate moments.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, these books are literally magickal and only work because the creator left a bit of themself in it to help you expand your understanding and take in this new excellence, or Arete, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-03-2019, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:19:45-07:00","id":1302184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1302138#post1302138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So while the ST can say &quot;yes you can meet Thor in the High Umbra&quot;, what that actually MEANS has no fixed answer. Is he a true god? Does he exist to inspire faith? Or does he exist because of faith? Is he part of The One, an avatar or aspect of it? Is he a shared hallucination of the Mages who meet him? Is he a powerful Spirit that has learned to feed off of a religion? Did Germanic Mages/Sleepers create these &quot;Gods&quot;, deliberately or accidentally? So even the objective facts of the setting remain contentious points of debate and argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add a permutation to this, there was a really fun idea that came up in these forums that I think adds a lot to the game. If someone whose Avatar manifests as Thor meets High Umbrood Thor, it is a good thing* for HU Thor to recognize the character and know things only Avatar Thor could. Mechanically, Avatar Thor and Umbrood Thor are not the same thing, but why should that be an issue in a game of reality on the brink.<br /> <br /> *Not a mandatory thing, because it depends on the kind of game you want to play, but in my opinion it adds a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T07:55:18-07:00","id":1302213,"title":"","content":"Indeed. For a character that has a god as Avatar that teaches him stuff, it adds a lot if he isn't just ignored when he meets that god or it's servants under other forms.<br /> <br /> As an extension to this, it could be cool that when a shaman calls the fire spirits to use Forces 3 to make fire dance...fire spirits actually know they have been called. Gafflins are nearly everywhere. I don't think it would harm the game if they notice and correspond the attention regardless of the fact that Forces (rather than a Charm) was used. Heck, the spirits themselves can believe that they caused the effect...maybe they did, if you believe that the Umbra it's more than a shadow of the world and actually influences it, it's just that some mages aknowledge this and others don't.<br /> <br /> If the spirits aknowledge the shaman maybe his paradigm it's true...or maybe the spirits themselves are deluded or manipulative. On the other hand, it would be very jarring to be a shaman and having the spirits you called testifying that they didn't do shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-03-2019, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T08:17:39-07:00","id":1302217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1302213#post1302213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. For a character that has a god as Avatar that teaches him stuff, it adds a lot if he isn't just ignored when he meets that god or it's servants under other forms.<br /> <br /> As an extension to this, it could be cool that when a shaman calls the fire spirits to use Forces 3 to make fire dance...fire spirits actually know they have been called. Gafflins are nearly everywhere. I don't think it would harm the game if they notice and correspond the attention regardless of the fact that Forces (rather than a Charm) was used. Heck, the spirits themselves can believe that they caused the effect...maybe they did, if you believe that the Umbra it's more than a shadow of the world and actually influences it, it's just that some mages aknowledge this and others don't.<br /> <br /> If the spirits aknowledge the shaman maybe his paradigm it's true...or maybe the spirits themselves are deluded or manipulative. On the other hand, it would be very jarring to be a shaman and having the spirits you called testifying that they didn't do shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well from the Shaman's perspective, ALL of his magick might be Spirit magick; the other Spheres are manipulating healing spirits, transformation spirits, time spirits, fire spirits, rock spirits, water spirits, tech spirits... etc. etc.<br /> <br /> This is a neat little feature that some mages have; the Affinity Sphere is seen as the source of all their Magick. For Psychics and &quot;all reality is thought&quot; types, Mind plays this role. For &quot;everything is Data&quot; types, Data can play this role. For some, Entropy or Life are the core of everything, and justify all effects. If you think Chi manipulation is the core of all magick, then Prime fuels all power.<br /> <br /> M20 TRIES to talk about this sort of thing with the &quot;A Bit of Spirit?&quot; side-bar, but messes it up sadly. It talks about how Spirit becomes an optional flavour extra in all Sphere effects for some Shamans, but personally I think this is better:<br /> <br /> - You choose your Affinity Sphere, and you can (if you wish) use it to justify all effects. You do still, naturally, need to learn other Spheres. Yes, to your Mage, Mind should be a super-sphere that does everything. But even that practice involves learning other powers, simply for the sake of balance and consistency. You can see it as your mage learning to use a specific iteration of Mind that deals with a certain sort of delusion/reality/dream.<br /> <br /> - Your Affinity Sphere's rating is directly tied to your Arete, always. If you start at Arete 3 then you have to put 3 of your 6 dots into your Affinity Sphere, for example. This means you never spend EXP on your Affinity Sphere; it simply increases when you raise your Arete.<br /> <br /> This means that for flavour you can always say that you're using Mind/Spirit/etc. as the cause of an effect, and in-game manifestations can follow this. Spirit sight would reveal fire spirits dancing around in the fire created by a shaman, for example. This is all optional though, and not all mages need to justify all their effects using their Affinity Sphere of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T11:54:48-07:00","id":1302289,"title":"","content":"That does sort of assume that the Affinity Sphere will be the Mage's strongest sphere. A Psionicist who focuses on clairvoyance or telekinesis would probably specialize in Correspondence or Forces respectively. <br /> <br /> In general I just assume that flavor is flavor. A Shaman might see everything through the lens of spirits, may even visibly summon them for every effect, but if the effect is just creating a fireball then they just need the spheres for a fireball. Likewise the Technocrat doesn't need Forces to power his spacial distortion unit just because it runs on electricity or cosmic radiation. The forces may be present but they aren't part of the effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T15:24:36-07:00","id":1302358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300972-four-levels-of-paradigm?p=1302289#post1302289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does sort of assume that the Affinity Sphere will be the Mage's strongest sphere. A Psionicist who focuses on clairvoyance or telekinesis would probably specialize in Correspondence or Forces respectively.<br /> <br /> In general I just assume that flavor is flavor. A Shaman might see everything through the lens of spirits, may even visibly summon them for every effect, but if the effect is just creating a fireball then they just need the spheres for a fireball. Likewise the Technocrat doesn't need Forces to power his spacial distortion unit just because it runs on electricity or cosmic radiation. The forces may be present but they aren't part of the effect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not assuming that Affinity Sphere will be the strongest Sphere, I'm saying that the Affinity Sphere is the strongest Sphere by tying it to Arete. To be clear, I'm saying that one approach is to simply tie Affinity Sphere and Arete together, so that the Mage will always be in a position where their 'Paradigm Sphere' so-to-speak is at a high enough level to justify whatever they're trying to do with the other spheres in terms of flavour. It also makes which Sphere you choose as Affinity slightly more significant, and also means that when you increase Arete you immediately gain access to some new abilities that can drive an important story moment etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}